  "difficulty_reason": "Supplying the named Sarkisov presentation and Hilbert90 prerequisites leaves the authored local construction of Galois-compatible affine representatives and a splitting-field-independent determinant. The new core proves invariance under changes of link representatives, constructs the six-link hexagon with typed neighbor data, calculates determinants for equal and unequal3-point classes using explicit matrices and norms, and descends the degree6 cases. The original5.21 then constructs the homomorphism on the full two-object birational groupoid and proves nontriviality using the non-norm parameter and a descended automorphism, so the selected obligation depends on substantial arithmetic birational geometry beyond ordinary qualification presentations.",
